      "output": "Hub Initialized: true\nActive Services Registered: 5\nCapstone Hub Topology Audit:\n -> INITIALIZING: PinIT Milestone 10 Event-Driven Microservices Hub\n -> SERVICE_READY: [orderService] Status=ONLINE Details={\"status\":\"ONLINE\",\"database\":\"PostgreSQL_Orders\"}\n -> SERVICE_READY: [paymentService] Status=ONLINE Details={\"status\":\"ONLINE\",\"database\":\"PostgreSQL_Payments\"}\n -> SERVICE_READY: [inventoryService] Status=ONLINE Details={\"status\":\"ONLINE\",\"database\":\"PostgreSQL_Inventory\"}\n -> SERVICE_READY: [kafkaCluster] Status=ONLINE Details={\"status\":\"ONLINE\",\"brokers\":3,\"partitions\":6}\n -> SERVICE_READY: [redisCluster] Status=ONLINE Details={\"status\":\"ONLINE\",\"slots\":16384,\"nodes\":3}",
      example: "In practice, when implementing Capstone Architecture Blueprint: The Unified Event-Driven Microservices Hub, an engineering or financial team first captures Capstone and validates Architecture against Blueprint before committing Unified. Event-driven microservices communicate asynchronously via durable event brokers, preventing cascading latency failures and enabling autonomous scaling across microservice boundaries.",
